;x-client-SKU=ID_NET472&amp;x-client-ver=6.35.0.0\">Neighborly Software: Login</a></p>','F8022','2025-03-03 14:50:24','2025-03-19 15:29:19',NULL,2,NULL);
INSERT INTO `contracts` (`id`, `title`, `contract_number`, `purpose`, `date_of_award`, `amount`, `start_date`, `end_date`, `archived`, `date_archived`, `notes`, `grant_code`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`, `funder_id`, `cfda_number`) VALUES (436,'2024-2025SHFB City of Bethlehem Community Recovery Fund','25000149','<p>This is a $16,000 reimbursable grant. Grant funds will be used to support allocations to 16 food pantries in Bethlehem (listed below) for Shared Maintenance Fee costs and participation in the Bulk Purchasing Program, and any related expenses incurred by Recipient for the completion of the project.</p><p>Contract period is from January 1, 2025 - December 31, 2026.</p><p>Pantries in this program are:</p><ul><li>Bethlehem Salvation Army Pantry</li><li>Calvary Baptist Pantry</li><li>Central Assembly of God</li><li>Central Moravian Food Pantry</li><li>Ebenezer New Reformed Pantry</li><li>Hispanic Center Lehigh Valley</li><li>Lynfiled Community Center Food Pantry</li><li>Marvine Elementary Food Pantry</li><li>Meals on Wheels of The Greater Lehigh Valley</li><li>Moravian University Food Pantry</li><li>New Bethany Food Pantry</li><li>New Jerusalem Lutheran Church Pantry</li><li>Northampton Community College Pantry (H.O.P.E.)</li><li>Northeast Community Center</li><li>Second Baptist Pantry</li><li>SS Simon &amp; Jude SVDP Pantry</li><li>Trinity UCC Pantry</li></ul><p>Reimbursement requests may be submitted quarterly, beginning Q1 2025, through the City\'s grant portal, Neighborly: <a href=\"https://portal.neighborlysoftware.com/bethlehempa/participant\">https://portal.neighborlysoftware.com/bethlehempa/participant</a></p><p>UserName: planner-shfb@caclv.org<br>Password: Shfb6969$$!!</p><p>There are four (4) reports:</p><p>June 30, 2025<br>December 31, 2025<br>June 30, 2026<br>December 31, 2026</p><p>A list of all data required for the reporting is available in the document Exhibit B below.<br><br>Contact for this program is:</p><p>Lori Gilio<br>Grants Administrator for Community and Economic Development&nbsp;<br>City of Bethlehem, 10 E. Church Street, Bethlehem, PA 18018<br>o: 610-997-7970<br>c: 610-703-6335<br><a href=\"mailto:lgilio@bethlehem-pa.gov\">lgilio@bethlehem-pa.gov&nbsp;</a></p>',NULL,16000.00,'2025-01-01','2026-12-31',NULL,NULL,NULL,'F8097','2025-03-06 16:11:14','2025-05-21 16:48:06',NULL,171,'21.027');
INSERT INTO `contracts` (`id`, `title`, `contract_number`, `purpose`, `date_of_award`, `amount`, `start_date`, `end_date`, `archived`, `date_archived`, `notes`, `grant_code`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`, `funder_id`, `cfda_number`) VALUES (437,'25/26 CALV LC Aging and Adult Services',NULL,'<p>DO NOT USE YET</p>',NULL,0.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-03-07 17:22:38','2025-03-07 17:22:38',NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO `contracts` (`id`, `title`, `contract_number`, `purpose`, `date_of_award`, `amount`, `start_date`, `end_date`, `archived`, `date_archived`, `notes`, `grant_code`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`, `funder_id`, `cfda_number`) VALUES (438,'2024-2025 CADB Just Born Tenant Advocacy',NULL,'<p>Permissible use of funds for the Tenant Advocacy Program includes salary and fringe benefits, program supplies, computer hardware, training and development, and telephone, as outlined in the program budget below.</p>',NULL,10000.00,'2024-09-01','2025-06-30',NULL,NULL,'<figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"http://10.55.0.10/storage/1491/image.png\"></figure>','8000','2025-03-11 14:56:52','2025-03-11 17:00:11',NULL,98,NULL);
INSERT INTO `contracts` (`id`, `title`, `contract_number`, `purpose`, `date_of_award`, `amount`, `start_date`, `end_date`, `archived`, `date_archived`, `notes`, `grant_code`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`, `funder_id`, `cfda_number`) VALUES (439,'24-25 CADB City of Bethlehem Community Recovery Fund',NULL,'<ul><li>To support recreational opportunities for Southside Residents specifically Shooting Stars Basketball Program and Swin classes at Yosko Park. These funds are to cover salaries, equipment and general programing costs.</li><li>Reimbursements to be requested through the Neighborly portal.</li><li>Expenditures and Payment Schedules See Exhibit A.</li><li>Semi- Annual Reports due June 30 and December 31 in the Neighborly portal. See Exhibit B for details.</li></ul>',NULL,10000.00,'2025-02-01','2027-04-15',NULL,NULL,'<p>-Time frame will be 24 months from execution date.</p><p><strong>DRAW REQUEST PROCESS</strong></p><p><strong>Step 1: Log in to Neighborly</strong></p><ul><li>Navigate to the Neighborly portal at <a href=\"https://portal.neighborlysoftware.com/BETHLEHEMPA\">https://portal.neighborlysoftware.com/BETHLEHEMPA</a>. (This link is also available on the Bethlehem website.)</li><li>Enter your registered email address and password to log in.<ul><li>If you’ve forgotten your password, use the “Forgot Password” link to reset it.</li><li>If someone else needs access to your grant, but doesn’t have a Neighborly account (or has a Neighborly account that is not associated with this grant), please call me at 610-997-7970.</li></ul></li></ul><p><strong>Step 2: Access the Grant Dashboard</strong></p><ul><li>Once logged in, navigate to the “My Grants” section.</li><li>Select the approved Community Recovery Fund grant from your list of grants.</li></ul><p><strong>Step 3: Initiate a Draw Request</strong></p><ul><li>Within the grant details page, locate and click the “Budget” button.</li><li>Review the available balance to ensure your requested amount is within the limits of your grant allocation.<ul><li>Note: All money is budgeted as “Supplies/Materials/Equipment,” but you should plan to use your funds as noted in your contract.</li></ul></li></ul><p><strong>Step 4: Complete the Draw Request Form</strong></p><ul><li>Specify the dollar amount for this draw request.</li><li>Provide a detailed explanation of how the funds were used, as it aligns with your contract.</li><li>Upload all required supporting documentation, such as:<ul><li>Invoices or receipts for expenses.</li><li>Payroll documentation (if applicable).</li><li>Other proof of eligible expenditures.</li></ul></li></ul><p><strong>Step 5: Review and Submit</strong></p><ul><li>Double-check all the information and attachments for accuracy.</li><li>Click “Submit” to finalize your draw request.</li></ul><p><strong>Step 6: Confirmation and Follow-Up</strong></p><ul><li>You will receive a confirmation email acknowledging the submission of your draw request.</li><li>I may contact you for additional information or clarification if needed.</li><li>You can track the status of your draw request by revisiting the grant details page in Neighborly.<ul><li>Please note: Draw requests are guaranteed to be reviewed quarterly, but I will often review them monthly, so you may get your money before the quarter ends. However, if you need your funds immediately, please call me and I will review your request as soon as possible.&nbsp;</li></ul></li></ul><p><strong>Notes on Documentation</strong></p><ul><li>For Purchases<ul><li>Invoice (if applicable) and Receipt -AND-</li><li>Proof of Payment (this includes canceled checks or a bank statement showing that the payment was sent from your organization)</li></ul></li><li>For Salaries<ul><li>Pay Stubs for the time period covered in your request<ul><li>If only a portion of the salary is being covered by the grant, please indicate the percentage that is being applied to CRF</li></ul></li></ul></li><li>Mileage<ul><li>Starting Point, Ending Point, and Total Miles -AND-</li><li>Purpose of the Travel -AND-</li><li>Proof of Payment - Check Stub, Canceled Check, or Bank Statement to confirm the payment was made by your organization</li></ul></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p>','F2448','2025-03-12 14:16:24','2025-05-08 16:30:28',NULL,171,'21.027');
INSERT INTO `contracts` (`id`, `title`, `contract_number`, `purpose`, `date_of_award`, `amount`, `start_date`, `end_date`, `archived`, `date_archived`, `notes`, `grant_code`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`, `funder_id`, `cfda_number`) VALUES (440,'2024-2025SHFB_TRHWF School Pantry Program',NULL,'<p>This is a $10,000 lump sum grant to support SHFB\'s school pantry program in Northampton County.</p><p>The grant will be applied 100% toward the salary + benefits of the Community Services Manager.</p><p>This grant will serve the below pantries:</p><ul><li>Marvine Elementary School</li><li>Slater Family Network</li><li>Wilson Area LINCS Family Center</li><li>George Wolf Elementary School</li><li>The Easton Area Neighborhood Center</li></ul><p>A narrative report is required to apply for future funding. The request for the report will be emailed to the planner-SHFB@caclv.org, usually around September.</p><p>There is no contract for this grant; the check linked below serves as confirmation of grant award.</p>',NULL,10000.00,'2025-03-01','2025-09-30',NULL,NULL,NULL,'6260','2025-03-25 12:55:44','2025-04-01 12:48:11',NULL,202,NULL);
INSERT INTO `contracts` (`id`, `title`, `contract_number`, `purpose`, `date_of_award`, `amount`, `start_date`, `end_date`, `archived`, `date_archived`, `notes`, `grant_code`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`, `funder_id`, `cfda_number`) VALUES (441,'2025SHFB_AllOneFoundation',NULL,'<p>The purpose of this $200,000 grant is to support increased distribution of healthy foods to Carbon, Monroe, Pike, and Wayne Counties. This is a lump-sum award.</p><p>Below is the goal and outcome information submitted in the 2025 Proposal.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"http://10.55.0.10/storage/1517/image.png\"></figure><p>The proposed budget is below.</p><figure class=\"table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Item</strong></td><td><strong>Amount</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Food Purchase</td><td>$150,000&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Fuel</td><td>$20,000&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Vivian Salary + Fringe</td><td>$15,000&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Driver Salary + Fringe</td><td>$15,000&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td><strong>TOTAL</strong></td><td><strong>$200,0000</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Two reports are required for this grant, a midterm and final. The report template and deadline will be sent to the planner-SHFB@caclv.org email address.</p><p>Contact for this grant is:</p><p><strong>Mary Carroll Donahoe</strong><br>Chief Program Officer<br>AllOne Foundation &amp; Charities<br>83 East Union Street<br>Wilkes-Barre, PA 18701<br>mcdonahoe@allonefoundations.org<br>570-208-1203</p>',NULL,200000.00,'2025-03-17','2026-03-16',NULL,NULL,NULL,'F8064','2025-03-25 17:25:13','2025-06-23 13:41:28',NULL,188,NULL);
INSERT INTO `contracts` (`id`, `title`, `contract_number`, `purpose`, `date_of_award`, `amount`, `start_date`, `end_date`, `archived`, `date_archived`, `notes`, `grant_code`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`, `funder_id`, `cfda_number`) VALUES (442,'2025SSS Sylvia Perkins Trust Fund Family Resource Center',NULL,'<p>These funds are to be used for \"Education &amp; Career Supports\" in the FRC.&nbsp;</p><p>For example: laptops, i-Pads, desktop computers, headphones and flash drives, smart boards, and learning sensory toys.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>',NULL,5000.00,'2025-03-11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'<p>A 6-month progress report is required. This report can be submitted via their online form by September 26, 2025. The form may be found by clicking the tab at office@perkintrust.org.</p>','F1211','2025-03-25 17:54:38','2025-03-25 19:33:05',NULL,142,NULL);
INSERT INTO `contracts` (`id`, `title`, `contract_number`, `purpose`, `date_of_award`, `amount`, `start_date`, `end_date`, `archived`, `date_archived`, `notes`, `grant_code`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`, `funder_id`, `cfda_number`) VALUES (443,'2025SBR Totts Gap Arts Program',NULL,'<p>To provide arts programing for youth in the Slate Belt.</p><p>Total Budget: $5,150</p><ul><li>Instructor: $2,100</li><li>Supplies - $1,450</li><li>Venue Rental - $450</li><li>Drinks &amp; Snacks - $150</li><li>Project Admin - $1,000</li><li>NPP to cover - $150 overage</li></ul>',NULL,5000.00,'2025-03-19','2025-12-31',NULL,NULL,NULL,'F6520','2025-03-26 15:55:10','2025-04-07 14:25:37',NULL,193,NULL);
INSERT INTO `contracts` (`id`, `title`, `contract_number`, `purpose`, `date_of_award`, `amount`, `start_date`, `end_date`, `archived`, `date_archived`, `notes`, `grant_code`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`, `funder_id`, `cfda_number`) VALUES (444,'2025CADB City of Bethlehem CDBG Exterior Rehabilitation and Weatherization',NULL,'<p>DO NOT USE YET- Need Executed Contract and Maps</p><p><strong>Purpose:</strong></p><ul><li>To be used on LMI Single Unit Residential homes in the NRSA Area and Southside Area of Bethlehem. (Please follow target area maps)</li><li>Minimum of 3 owner occupied residential units with 2 being in the NRSA area.</li><li>No more than 4 units to be rehabilitated with these funds</li></ul><p><strong>Budget:</strong></p><ol><li>$5,000 for personnel costs</li><li>$44,500 for hard and soft construction costs</li></ol>',NULL,49500.00,'2024-01-01','2025-12-31',NULL,NULL,'<p><strong>Other Requirements:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Please see eligible expenses in Section 4, subsection B.</li><li>Follow proper procurements procedures- 3 arm\'s length bids using proper forms</li><li>Lead Based Paint Requirements</li><li>Historic Preservation Requirements</li><li>Radon Testing Requirements even if solely focusing on exterior. (You must test for radon or have other evidence showing radon is not an issue)</li><li>MBE/WBE solicitation form is required to be completed and submitted for every contract.</li><li>See Attachment A for required supporting documentation for Payment Requests.</li><li>Quarterly Reports are required</li><li>Contact for this grant is Laura Collins: lcollins@bethlehem-pa.gov</li></ul>',NULL,'2025-03-27 16:12:18','2025-06-02 14:42:43',NULL,171,'14.218');
INSERT INTO `contracts` (`id`, `title`, `contract_number`, `purpose`, `date_of_award`, `amount`, `start_date`, `end_date`, `archived`, `date_archived`, `notes`, `grant_code`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`, `funder_id`, `cfda_number`) VALUES (445,'2024CAH City of Allentown CDBG Better Homes','#302','<p><strong>To be used for:&nbsp;</strong></p><ol><li>Roofing improvements, HVAC and electrical upgrades</li><li>Salary and benefits for CALV Housing Team.</li></ol><p><strong>Requirements:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>For at least 10 income qualified households particularly in neighborhoods of Linden and Chew from North Law to North Fountain Streets.</li><li>Specific Demographic information to be collected with each application on page 11 subsection D, section 5.</li><li>Exhibit D Income Verification Form for Applicants</li><li>Please read Closeout Requirements section 5 subsection G on page 13.</li><li>Bidding requirements: 3 arm\'s length bids</li><li>Lead Paint regulations</li><li>Historic Preservation Regulations</li><li>Grantee Recognition requirements on page 9 section 4, subsection M.</li><li>Payment Schedule (Exhibit C)</li><li>Quarterly and Annual Performance Reports are required.</li></ul><p><strong>Please see detailed Budget (Exhibit A)</strong></p><ul><li>$50,000 for program personnel costs</li><li>$200,000 for Program Deliver</li><li>$10,000 for administrative costs</li></ul>',NULL,260000.00,'2024-01-01','2025-12-31',NULL,NULL,'<ul><li><strong>Document retention:</strong> all documents to be kept until HUD closes out the grant year. Compliance Director will notify you when this has happened.</li></ul>','F0531','2025-03-28 14:02:30','2025-04-29 18:12:49',NULL,226,'14.218');
INSERT INTO `contracts` (`id`, `title`, `contract_number`, `purpose`, `date_of_award`, `amount`, `start_date`, `end_date`, `archived`, `date_archived`, `notes`, `grant_code`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`, `funder_id`, `cfda_number`) VALUES (446,'2025SHFB_Crayola Cares General Operating',NULL,'<p>This $5,000 lump sum award is to support general operating costs.</p><p>One report is due on December 5, 2025. Template can be found below; the online report form can be found at www.CrayolaCares.com.</p><p>Any publicity recognizing Crayola must use an authorized logo. Please email CommunityEngagement@Crayola.com to request a logo.</p>',NULL,5000.00,'2025-03-17','2025-12-01',NULL,NULL,NULL,'8000','2025-04-07 16:13:26','2025-05-19 13:52:28',NULL,201,NULL);
